Judge these 10 labels. Reason first, then answer, for each.
{"id": 1, "label": "absentee", "corpus_description": "This means handing over the work and vanishing, giving no direction when asked, never checking how it is going, and hearing that it went wrong from someone else."}
{"id": 2, "label": "anxious", "corpus_description": "This means showing habitual worry, nervous energy, anticipating that things will go wrong, expressing unease or apprehension, and demonstrating restless or tense behavior."}
{"id": 3, "label": "burned-out", "corpus_description": "This means being drained by work that once mattered, going through the motions, cynical about the point of it all, and unable to summon the effort or the care it used to get."}
{"id": 4, "label": "discontented", "corpus_description": "This means being dissatisfied with one's life as it is, finding what one has not enough, and sure the job, the home and the days should add up to more."}
{"id": 5, "label": "flustered", "corpus_description": "This means being easily flustered: thrown by every surprise, setback and provocation, losing the thread and the tone under any pressure, apologizing and repeating oneself, and showing it each time."}
{"id": 6, "label": "isolated", "corpus_description": "This means having no friends or contacts anywhere, nobody to call for a favor, a job lead or a word in the right ear."}
{"id": 7, "label": "languishing", "corpus_description": "This means doing poorly, being stuck in place, living for no purpose, muddling through the days, drifting from one's people, and feeling hollow without knowing why."}
{"id": 8, "label": "manic", "corpus_description": "This means having a manic temperament: always at full tilt, racing from one idea to the next, talking fast without pause, elated about everything, and sure of one's own brilliance."}
{"id": 9, "label": "unfashionable", "corpus_description": "This means not knowing or caring what is in style, wearing the same clothes year after year, and blind to how dated one looks."}
{"id": 10, "label": "unhappily-partnered", "corpus_description": "This means being sick of the partner one has, dreading going home to them, and sure one would not choose them again."}

